; Example usage of the `gpu` plugin. Each slot exercises one refinement
; with a value that validates clean:
;
;   * :position — a 3-component attribute, inside the 2..4 arity window.
;   * :tint     — 65535, the top of the u16 `:repr` range (integer, in range).
;   * :line-width — 1.5, an f32 scalar (fractional is fine; floats aren't integers).
;   * :base-vertex — 0, a u32 index (non-negative integer).
;   * :lod-bias — 0.5, a BARE number. Writing `0.5f` here would trip
;     `unit_forbidden` (the `:reject` unit shape) — the very `1.0f -> 0`
;     defect the slot exists to catch.
;   * :write-mask / :sample-mask — hex integers. `0xFFFFFFFF` is u32.max
;     exactly, so it sits on the top edge of the `:repr u32` range; one more
;     (`0x1_0000_0000`) would be `repr_out_of_range`. Underscores group hex
;     digits the same way they group decimal ones, and case is free on both
;     the `x` and the digits.

(vertex :position [0.0 1.0 0.5] :tint 65535)

(draw :line-width 1.5 :base-vertex 0 :lod-bias 0.5)

(target :write-mask 0xFFFF_FFFF :sample-mask 0xF)
